# Line ending normalization.
#
# This repository previously had MIXED line endings committed (some files CRLF,
# some LF) with no .gitattributes, which meant:
#   - `mix format` rewrote every CRLF file to LF (~6,500 lines of noise per run)
#   - `mix format --check-formatted` could NEVER pass
#   - `format` had to be excluded from the verify/precommit aliases
#
# The Elixir formatter always writes LF, so the working tree is normalized to LF
# too (`eol=lf`, not just `text=auto`). That keeps the working tree, the
# repository, and the formatter consistent, and lets formatting rejoin the gate.
#
# See DEVELOPMENT.md ("Line endings & formatting").
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert, never attempt a text diff.
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.svg   text
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.so    binary
*.dll   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary

# Windows shell scripts must keep CRLF to execute reliably.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
